 "notes": "Observed 95% CL upper limit (solid crimson curve) from Fig. 10, extracted from the vector PDF in the arXiv e-print (ALP_joint_upper_limits_redshifted_DSNALPB_flux_w_HeavyNuclei_Mfail_20percent_statistical_uncertainty.pdf). Benchmark scenario: f_fail-CC=20%, Salpeter IMF, fiducial SFR, Jansson12c Galactic magnetic field model, Lorimer I interstellar emission model; 12-yr Fermi-LAT template analysis of the diffuse SN ALP background. Flat level g_agamma = 3.77e-11 GeV^-1 matches the quoted 3.76e-11 GeV^-1 for m_a << 1e-11 eV; flat limit extended to the figure's left edge at 1e-12 eV. Curve clipped at the figure's top frame (g=1e-9 GeV^-1) near m_a ~ 1e-8 eV. Astrophysical bound, no dark-matter density assumption. Systematic variations (Fig. 11) change the limit by up to ~factor 2; Fig. 10 benchmark is the headline result.",
